Yes, your code is now **perfectly configured** for a production-ready application. You have successfully:

1.  **Connected to Firebase** with your real API keys.
2.  **Enabled Analytics** to track your visitors.
3.  **Switched to Cloud Storage** (Firestore) so your data is safe and accessible from any device.
4.  **Secured the Admin Panel** so only `admin@wrsmile.com` can manage products.

### **Final Step: Secure Your Database**
Before you publish, you must update your **Firestore Security Rules** in the Firebase Console. If you don't do this, either the app won't work, or hackers could delete your products.

1.  Go to [Firebase Console](https://console.firebase.google.com) > **Firestore Database** > **Rules**.
2.  Delete the existing rules and paste this **exact code** to secure your shop:

```groovy
rules_version = '2';
service cloud.firestore {
  match /databases/{database}/documents {

    // 1. Users: Users can only read/write their own profile
    match /users/{userId} {
      allow read, write: if request.auth != null && request.auth.uid == userId;
    }

    // 2. Products: Everyone can read, only Admin can write
    match /products/{productId} {
      allow read: if true;
      allow write: if request.auth != null && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)).data.role == 'admin';
    }

    // 3. Orders: Users can read/create their own orders. Admin can read/update all.
    match /orders/{orderId} {
      // Anyone can create an order (even guests, needed for your WhatsApp flow initially)
      allow create: if true;

      // Users can read their own orders, Admins can read all
      allow read: if request.auth != null && (
        resource.data.userEmail == request.auth.token.email || 
        get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)).data.role == 'admin'
      );

      // Only Admins can update status (e.g., mark as delivered)
      allow update: if request.auth != null && get(/databases/$(database)/documents/users/$(request.auth.uid)).data.role == 'admin';
    }
  }
}
